{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "ODD is the graph-native product-authoring method for GTL/ABG domain products. Its structural carriers are typed domain assets, named graph functions, a published function catalog, an operative GTL module, ABG-owned execution, a constructive evaluation loop, and current-state projections over constructive history.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1846,
          "quote": "ODD method is the graph-native product-authoring method for building GTL/ABG domain products.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F20.%20Canonical%20Compression",
          "start_line": 1846
        }
      ],
      "key": "odd_method",
      "label": "ODD method"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Applies to every ODD product over GTL/ABG."],
      "definition": "The method-level homeostasis loop connects intent lineage and model synthesis, observation, gap pressure, exact target binding, lawful action selection, admitted construction and evidence, fulfillment and closure, and subsequent lawful action.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 868,
          "quote": "Every ODD product over GTL/ABG must preserve one constructive evaluation loop\nfrom intent lineage and model synthesis through observation to next lawful\naction.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 862
        }
      ],
      "key": "constructive_evaluation_loop",
      "label": "Constructive evaluation loop"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The selected Product outcome under STDO-UP-013 is external authority for the loop. An admitted bounded prerequisite or experiment may also supply a bounded work basis. Models, gaps, assurance, ledgers and projections interpret these bases but do not author, select or enlarge the outcome.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 874,
          "quote": "The selected Product outcome under `STDO-UP-013` is external authority for this\nloop. Product models, gaps, assurance, ledgers, and projections may interpret\nthat outcome but cannot author, select, or enlarge it.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 870
        }
      ],
      "key": "selected_product_outcome",
      "label": "Selected Product outcome and bounded bases"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "IntentLineage is admitted source intent with human, imported-source, prior-product, intent-engine or prior synthesized-intent lineage, held as ABG event-log truth. ProductAssetModel is desired and known typed asset truth synthesized from lineage, prior model and admitted product truth, with admitted publication events and product projection references; it is neither runtime fact nor action authority. Worksite is observable workspace, runtime archive, transform assets, product asset root, profile and file/process state. RuntimeEventLog is append-only admitted runtime facts; RuntimeProjection is replay-derived current runtime state over that log and execution basis. ObservationSnapshot is a read-only runtime/worksite view carried by the ABG evaluator with product domain rows. GapPressureRow describes missing, partial, blocked, waiting or ambiguous asset/evidence pressure relative to the model.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 923,
          "quote": "| `ObservationSnapshot` | Read-only view of runtime truth plus worksite facts relevant to construction. | ABG evaluator carrier with product domain rows. |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 917
        }
      ],
      "key": "loop_observation_carriers",
      "label": "Intent, model, runtime and observation carriers"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "TargetObligationBinding exactly binds gap pressure to the selected Product outcome, any admitted prerequisite/experiment basis, target assets, required roles, evidence references and admissible graph outcomes. ActionCatalog publishes lawful graph functions, vectors, targets, inputs and eligible outcomes. PriorityProjection deterministically ranks bound lawful actions under visible policy. ConstructionIntent is an admitted selected action for one bounded graph invocation preserving outcome/bounded-basis references. NextActionProjection reads NextActionBasis and current truth to select a next graph action only when lawful. These are product domain bindings and policy over GTL/ABG publication, admission and traversal authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 932,
          "quote": "| `TargetObligationBinding` | Exact binding from gap pressure to the selected Product outcome, any admitted prerequisite or experiment basis, target assets, required roles, evidence refs, and admissible graph outcomes. | Product domain binding over GTL/ABG action authority. |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 924
        }
      ],
      "key": "loop_action_carriers",
      "label": "Binding, catalog, intent and action projections"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "AdmittedEvidence comprises admitted worker, process, product, execution, materialization, liveness and postflight evidence, not worker self-closure. EdgeFulfillmentLedger carries closure evidence and convergence for one edge attempt/version, including counts, obligation rows, materialization/liveness/admission references and edge_converged. EdgeClosureDecision is the sum type close, yield, retry, repair, re-enter, reprice or block. NextActionBasis is the dispatch sum initial_selection, post_yield_resume, post_close_graph_continuation, post_retry, post_repair, post_reenter, post_reprice or post_block; it is not another controller, and post_reprice carries no action-selection authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 931,
          "quote": "| `EdgeClosureDecision` | Sum type over the ledger: close, yield, retry, repair, re-enter, reprice, block. | Closure decision truth. |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 926
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1170,
          "quote": "counts\nobligation rows\nmaterialization refs\nliveness refs\nadmission refs\nedge_converged",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 1165
        }
      ],
      "key": "loop_closure_carriers",
      "label": "Evidence, fulfillment, closure and continuation basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "synthesize_model maps IntentLineage, prior ProductAssetModel and admitted product truth to ProductAssetModel. eval_gap maps ProductAssetModel, RuntimeEventLog, RuntimeProjection and Worksite to ObservationSnapshot and GapPressureRow. evaluate_next maps NextActionBasis, fresh eval_gap, TargetObligationBinding, ActionCatalog and Policy to PriorityProjection, NextActionProjection and selected_action or typed no-action. evaluate_action maps ConstructionIntent, AdmittedEvidence, TargetObligationBinding and Policy to EdgeFulfillmentLedger and EdgeClosureDecision.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 936,
          "quote": "The loop has one model synthesis function and three distinct evaluation\nfunctions. They may share underlying libraries, but they must not share\nauthority:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 934
        }
      ],
      "key": "four_function_surface",
      "label": "Four-function computational surface"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The governed work pair consists of mutable workspace W, immutable ledger L of admitted closure-relevant work over W, immutable ordering/replay event spine E, and evaluator work Ev over a declared L snapshot. L is an admitted trace, not a workspace copy: it records callout basis, deltas, file references, digests, execution evidence, obligations, claims, evaluator inputs/outputs and admission status. Ledger attention is a structural analogy to attention, not a transformer implementation dependency.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1007,
          "quote": "W = mutable workspace under construction\nL = immutable governed ledger of work over W\nE = immutable event log / replay spine\nEv = evaluator work over L",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 997
        },
        {
          "end_line": 1056,
          "quote": "This is a structural analogy, not an implementation dependency on transformer\nattention.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20Evaluation%20And%20Yield%20Loop",
          "start_line": 1053
        }
      ],
      "key": "governed_work_pair",
      "label": "Workspace, ledger, event spine and evaluator work"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Manual walkthrough is the human-explainable traversal of the same declared process as automation: identify current typed asset/node; identify the next lawful vector and public graph-function carrier; determine inputs, evaluators, output contract and carried environment; construct or assess the next asset/checkpoint; repeat to target-relative closure. The vector is the constitutional transition contract; the graph function is its published constructive realization.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1490,
          "quote": "A human operator, using only the declared authority surfaces, should be able to:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.7%20Manual%20Walkthrough%20Must%20Still%20Be%20Lawful",
          "start_line": 1484
        }
      ],
      "key": "manual_walkthrough",
      "label": "Manual walkthrough"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Agentic conformance has an F_P walkthrough proving process followability and an F_D gate admitting produced artifacts. The agent reasons, drafts and proposes from the smallest sufficient declared authority packet with source references. SPEC_METHOD owns the general constitutional process and TICKET_METHOD artifact admission; ODD specializes and composes those laws.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1517,
          "quote": "Conformance has two halves: an F_P proof that the process is followable, and an F_D gate that admits the produced artifacts.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.7A%20Conforming%20Agentic%20Development",
          "start_line": 1517
        }
      ],
      "key": "agentic_conformance",
      "label": "Agentic conformance"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["For negative proof of an ODD or graph-native boundary."],
      "definition": "Closure-grade negative proof exercises the supported Product authority path after invalidating its real authority-bearing input. Where the named identities apply, that path is public entry → admitted GTL composition owning topology → named GraphFunction callable contract → implementation/plugin limited to its admitted seam → ABG traversal/event/continuation/replay truth → replay projection → typed Product outcome or continuation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1570,
          "quote": "Closure-grade negative evidence identifies the supported entry and governing\nauthority, invalidates the real authority-bearing input, exercises the\nsupported path, proves refusal before the prohibited effect, and establishes\nthat no legacy, fallback, reconstruction, or parallel path succeeds.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F11.%20Core%20Law%2F11.7B%20Real%20Authority-Path%20Negative%20Proof%20%28%60STDO-UP-010%60%29",
          "start_line": 1566
        }
      ],
      "key": "negative_authority_path_proof",
      "label": "Real authority-path negative proof"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A scenario is a graph-native proving surface, beyond test documentation. Declared scenarios and use cases are described as the best source for significant proving/code/control paths because they pressure feature intent and design decisions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1643,
          "quote": "Scenarios are graph-native proving surfaces.\n\nThey are not only test documentation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F12.%20Scenario%20Rule",
          "start_line": 1641
        }
      ],
      "key": "scenario_bundle",
      "label": "Scenario bundle"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["When starting cold in a concrete ODD product."],
      "definition": "The cold-start route is an ordered acquisition route with general ODD and world-model specializations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1783,
          "quote": "When starting cold in a concrete ODD product, use this order.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/ODD_METHOD.md#ODD%20Method%2F18.%20Cold-Start%20Reading%20Order",
          "start_line": 1783
        }
      ],
      "key": "odd_cold_start_route",
      "label": "ODD cold-start reading route"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A post is repository working commentary for analysis, criticism, proposed changes, handoff or repricing confidence. It conveys observations and proposals, may influence specification/design, and is not constitutional truth; adoption remains an owning decision.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 15,
          "quote": "Posts are not constitutional truth. They are working commentary that may later influence specification or design.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide",
          "start_line": 15
        }
      ],
      "key": "commentary_post",
      "label": "Commentary post"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The post carrier is selected by the Product Definition Overlay's ticketing.comments.root binding. The default local-file root is .ai-workspace/comments/<agent>/; .ai-workspace/comments/<agent-id>/ is an example.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 56,
          "quote": "Posts live at the Product Definition Overlay's `ticketing.comments.root`\nbinding.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide%2FLocation",
          "start_line": 50
        }
      ],
      "key": "post_carrier",
      "label": "Bound post carrier"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The prescribed post categories are REVIEW: critique of code, spec, design or another post; STRATEGY: proposed technical/methodological direction; GAP: precise insufficiency/contradiction; SCHEMA: data/event model, interface or contract shape; HANDOFF: bounded context/task-state transfer; MATRIX: explicit comparison of options.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 100,
          "quote": "- `REVIEW` for critique of code, spec, design, or another post\n- `STRATEGY` for a proposed technical or methodological direction\n- `GAP` for a precise insufficiency or contradiction\n- `SCHEMA` for data model, event model, interface, or contract shape\n- `HANDOFF` for bounded transfer of context or task state\n- `MATRIX` for explicit decision comparison across options",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide%2FCategories",
          "start_line": 95
        }
      ],
      "key": "post_categories",
      "label": "Post categories"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The post base template has a CATEGORY: Subject title; Author, ISO 8601 Date, Addresses, Status initially Draft, optional ISO 8601 Updated; Summary, Analysis and Recommended Action sections. MATRIX uses a central decision table instead of free prose. This describes a template, not an instantiated post.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 124,
          "quote": "# {CATEGORY}: {Subject}\n\n**Author**: {agent}\n**Date**: {ISO 8601}\n**Addresses**: {artifact, issue, or boundary under discussion}\n**Status**: Draft\n**Updated**: {ISO 8601, optional}",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide%2FStructure",
          "start_line": 109
        }
      ],
      "key": "post_template",
      "label": "Post base template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Post discussion states are Draft, still shaped by its author; Open, published into active discussion; and Closed, discussion concluded. Closed describes stable commentary, not ratification.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 139,
          "quote": "- `Draft` for a post still being shaped by its author\n- `Open` for a post published into an active discussion\n- `Closed` for a post whose discussion has concluded",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide%2FDiscussion%20State%20And%20Mutability",
          "start_line": 137
        }
      ],
      "key": "post_discussion_state",
      "label": "Post discussion state"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Reusable method-change propagation preserves authority causality: incident/review evidence → shared-method intake → one owning standard → consistency and independent review → human-authority acceptance → one complete released STDO version → explicit consumer selection → consumer-owned realization and evidence. This is not a prescribed intake workflow or artifact set.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 200,
          "quote": "This is authority causality, not a prescribed intake workflow or artifact set.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/POSTING_GUIDE.md#Posting%20Guide%2FShared%20Method%20Adoption%20And%20Propagation%20%28%60STDO-UP-012%60%29",
          "start_line": 200
        }
      ],
      "key": "shared_method_propagation",
      "label": "Shared method adoption and propagation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Standards Library contains deciding methods, foundational contracts and non-deciding views. A complete cut also includes declared projections, schemas, templates, frames and interaction assets. A selectable release has one complete immutable constitutional member set with exact cut identity, manifest and membership. Source-line Product Definition identity and immutable Product/release identities retain distinct source-owned relations; subordinate executable/interaction tooling has separate responsibilities.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 10,
          "quote": "A selectable\nrelease has one complete immutable constitutional member set with exact cut\nidentity, manifest and membership.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/README.md#Standards%20Library",
          "start_line": 5
        }
      ],
      "key": "standards_library",
      "label": "Standards Library"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "As described by the library index, Foundations owns finite-capacity, interpretation, purpose, identity, typed-composition, total-handling and judgment/authority premises, the single result algebra and conjunction, workspace-derived context and configuration. Transformation Library owns shared contract application, constraint surfaces, faithful projection and composition, organized as Bind, Acquire, Transform, Evaluate, Conjoin and Dispose.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 25,
          "quote": "Bind, Acquire,\nTransform, Evaluate, Conjoin and Dispose organise these responsibilities.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/README.md#Standards%20Library%2FFoundations%20and%20shared%20library",
          "start_line": 24
        }
      ],
      "key": "shared_contract_owners",
      "label": "Indexed Foundations and Transformation Library responsibilities"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The method-owner index routes: formal carrier-neutral calculus to Axiomatic Calculus; generic frame law to Reference Frame Method and bounded-context term resolution to Spec; operational/specialist/Executive configurations to Baseline; constitutional WHAT/construction to Spec; structural HOW/transformation admission/realization to Design Module; names/exact identities to Identity; graph-native domain to ODD; optional application-neutral traversal model to Traversal Occurrence Profile; state/treatment/world-model claims to World Model; UX realization to UX; work governance to Ticket; exact cuts/conservation/publication/adoption protocol to Release, Product-definition routing to Spec and consumer adoption to consumer authority; commentary/writing to Posting/Writing Guides; discovery/locator resolution to Glossary.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 88,
          "quote": "Each member's declared applicability and scope remain at that owner; this table\ndoes not reclassify a constitutional method as a guide or profile.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/README.md#Standards%20Library%2FMethod%20owners",
          "start_line": 83
        }
      ],
      "key": "method_owner_index",
      "label": "Method-owner routing index"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Distribution includes digest-bound non-deciding compressions; starter templates for a per-Product Definition, project specifications, project frame basis and agent bootstrap; normative layout-neutral Product Definition Overlay and deterministic installed-release manifest schemas; routing interaction assets; complete immutable versioned cuts; projected frames; and an interpretation containing encoded determinations, source routes and unresolved conditions. Document-source and complete-package inventories are distinct.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 110,
          "quote": "Plugin interaction assets route work;\nthey mint no authority or workflow engine.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/README.md#Standards%20Library%2FDistribution%20and%20entry",
          "start_line": 109
        }
      ],
      "key": "distribution_and_entry_assets",
      "label": "Distribution and entry assets"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Reference Frame Method is the named source member for bounded frame reasoning and evaluation. Its source identity is retained separately from index references to it.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1,
          "quote": "# Reference Frame Method",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#Reference%20Frame%20Method",
          "start_line": 1
        }
      ],
      "key": "reference_frame_method",
      "label": "Reference Frame Method"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Finite actors have bounded context, attention, time and capability. An activated frame combines a declared evaluation family, exact workspace/topology basis, finite material relations/coordinates, applicable invariants/authorities, admissible evidence/exclusions and actor envelope. Its evaluated predicates use satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame or invalid_basis. Project engagement proceeds through human-informed frame-set declaration, bounded evaluations, required conjunction/translation, coverage with residual uncertainty, and empirical revision; these remain separate functions. An atomic engagement unit can contain multiple semantic atoms and owner relations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 45,
          "quote": "`Atomic engagement unit` names the unit that can be activated and evaluated as\none bounded context. It does not assert that every relation inside the frame is\none irreducible semantic atom.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#Reference%20Frame%20Method%2FCanonical%20Compression",
          "start_line": 42
        }
      ],
      "key": "bounded_frame_engagement",
      "label": "Bounded frame engagement and result domain"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An evaluation is a declared question with known predicate, admissible evidence, decision authority and, for material action, operation authority. Questions may concern judgment, prediction, construction, comparison, proof, refusal, classification or action recommendation. An evaluation family groups questions requiring the same material-relation manifold, authority basis and core-result binding/refinement; similar wording does not establish family identity.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 132,
          "quote": "An evaluation family groups questions that require the same material relation\nmanifold, authority basis, and result binding or refinement of that one algebra.\nSimilar wording does not prove that two evaluations belong to the same family.",
